WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.120
Chimpanzees have 48
chromosomes in each body cell.

2
00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:07.020
You have 46, two fewer.

3
00:00:07.070 --> 00:00:11.120
In both, they come in pairs:
one set from each parent.

4
00:00:11.170 --> 00:00:14.690
Photograph them in a dividing cell,
and you see a scatter of dark,

5
00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:17.700
stained rods, in no particular order.

6
00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:20.840
So how can you tell which
two belong together?

7
00:00:20.890 --> 00:00:25.720
In this mission, you'll find out what
makes two chromosomes a true matching pair,

8
00:00:25.770 --> 00:00:27.390
one from each parent.

9
00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:32.590
Then you'll pin down a gene's exact
address on a chromosome: its locus.

10
00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:37.250
Your mission: find out how to tell
which chromosomes make up each pair.
